1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
ANNA: Welcome to Ocean Talk. Today we look at rivers and plastic.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:30,000
ANNA: Most plastic in the sea starts its journey in a river, carried by rain from the streets.

3
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:20,000
TOM: In Jakarta, volunteers built floating barriers that stop bottles before they reach the sea.

4
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:30,000
TOM: Every barrier collects about two tonnes of rubbish a month, and students help to sort it for recycling.
